menu "HLS Player Configuration"

    config APP_HLS_PLAYER_RING_BUFFER_SIZE
        int "Ring buffer size (KB)"
        default 128 if SPIRAM
        default 64 if !SPIRAM
        range 32 256
        help
            Size of the ring buffer for streaming data in KB.

            Recommended values:
            - With PSRAM: 128-256 KB (better resilience to jitter)
            - Without PSRAM: 64-96 KB (balance RAM/stability)

            Larger buffer = more latency but more resilient to network jitter.

    config APP_HLS_PLAYER_REM_BUFFER_SIZE
        int "Remainder buffer size (KB) - P1.3 RAM optimization"
        default 8
        range 4 16
        help
            [RAM OPT P1.3] Small buffer to keep unconsumed bytes between decode cycles.

            This replaces the large encoded_buffer (144 KB → 8 KB = -136 KB gain).

            Recommended values:
            - 4 KB: Minimal, may increase decode errors if TS packets are large
            - 8 KB: Recommended (sufficient for AAC/TS, tested)
            - 16 KB: Conservative (if decode errors occur)

            Larger = more resilient to large TS packets, but more RAM.
            Typical remainder size observed: < 4 KB.

    config APP_HLS_PLAYER_DEC_BUFFER_SIZE
        int "Decoded buffer size (KB)"
        default 16
        range 8 32
        help
            Size of the output PCM buffer in KB.

            Default 16 KB is sufficient for most cases (48kHz stereo).
            Only increase if you experience audio glitches with high sample rates.

    config APP_HLS_PLAYER_DROP_OLD_ON_FULL
        bool "Drop old data when ring buffer full (recommended)"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, drops oldest chunk from ring buffer to make room for new data.
            This improves live-ness by keeping the stream fresh.

            When disabled, drops new data (classic behavior) which can cause temporal drift.

            Recommended: ENABLED for live streams, DISABLED for VOD.

endmenu
